WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.979
128 GB of VRAM

00:00:02.838 --> 00:00:03.604
on a tiny

00:00:03.416 --> 00:00:04.111
PC

00:00:04.638 --> 00:00:05.805
A homelabber hung

00:00:05.617 --> 00:00:06.902
four used 32

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:08.812
gigabyte Nvidia V100

00:00:08.624 --> 00:00:09.449
cards off a

00:00:09.261 --> 00:00:11.465
tiny Lenovo M720q

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.196
mini PC

00:00:12.397 --> 00:00:14.425
for 128 gigabytes

00:00:14.237 --> 00:00:15.298
of video memory

00:00:15.838 --> 00:00:17.052
A PCIe switch

00:00:16.864 --> 00:00:17.807
card fans out

00:00:17.619 --> 00:00:18.774
to four OCuLink

00:00:18.586 --> 00:00:19.305
cables

00:00:19.444 --> 00:00:20.422
A solder bridge

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:21.047
on the riser

00:00:20.859 --> 00:00:21.967
and coreboot got

00:00:21.779 --> 00:00:22.851
past a BIOS

00:00:22.663 --> 00:00:23.806
that only booted

00:00:23.618 --> 00:00:24.526
two cards

00:00:25.046 --> 00:00:25.906
The build hits

00:00:25.718 --> 00:00:27.781
about 285 tokens

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:28.560
per second in

00:00:28.371 --> 00:00:29.491
total on Qwen

00:00:29.315 --> 00:00:31.178
3.8 27B

00:00:31.402 --> 00:00:34.279
for roughly 3,500 dollars

00:00:34.806 --> 00:00:35.820
Full story on

00:00:35.631 --> 00:00:36.527
the dashboard
